    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Estate Agents are proud to present 14 Ballydowd Grove, a spacious detached family residence which boasts an enviable sunny South facing garden. Set in an exclusive, low-density development which is located only short walk from Lucan Village, this property is sure to appeal to those seeking their forever home in a most sought-after location. \n\n14 Ballydowd Grove measures a substantial 138 sq.m/1,485 sq.ft of light filled accommodation with further potential to extend if required. The property has been well maintained throughout and offers a chain free opportunity for the discerning purchasers.\n\nThe real garden is a real gem and a complete suntrap with an enviable South facing aspect. This garden is most private and laid in lawn with mature planting, hedging and tree's. The property is fully detached and benefits from gated pedestrian access on both sides of the property. Furthermore, there is a large gated front driveway and garden which has been beautifully cared for.\n\nBallydowd Grove is an exclusive and sought after residential development in the heart of Lucan village, ideally located just minutes from Lucan's host of cafés, restaurants, pubs and shops. Roselawn is readily accessible to both the M4 and M50 and is only a short stroll from a host of bus routes. Some of Dublin's finest primary and secondary schools are also within walking distance.\n\nLucan is a most sought-after Dublin suburb situated 13 km west of Dublin city centre. There are some fantastic leisure facilities in the area including GAA clubs, soccer clubs, water sports along the River Liffey and is home to some of Dublin's finest parks including St Catherine's Park, Griffeen Valley Park and the nearby Castletown House. Pheonix Park, the largest enclosed public park in any capital city in Europe, is less than a 15 minute drive away. There are fantastic primary and secondary schools in the Lucan area, including Gael Scoils. Located only a short drive from Liffey Valley Shopping Centre and close to a number of large multinational companies such as Pfizer, Aryzta, Takeda, Hewlett Packard and Intel.\n \nViewing comes highly recommended to appreciate all that is on offer in this terrific family home. Viewing by appointment via selling agents DNG Lucan, phone 01-6280400."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - 1.04m x 5.7m\nWelcoming entrance hallway with wood flooring and a hot linen press\n\nLiving Room - 4.66m x 5.84m\nSpacious living room to the front with an open fireplace, carpeted flooring and ceiling coving\n\nKitchen/Dining - 2.42m x 4.24m\nLight filled kitchen/dining with a fully fitted kitchen and access to the rear garden\n\nLounge - 2.4m x 4.03m\nLounge with carpeted flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.44m x 1.66m\nFully tiled bathroom with a bath, wc and whb\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.03m x 2.96m\nSpacious master bedroom to the rear with built in wardrobes and carpeted flooring\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.88m x 3.34m\nLarge double bedroom to the rear with carpeted flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nLanding - .94m x 2.65m\n\n\nShower Room - 1m x 2.31m\nTiled shower room with a shower, wc and whb\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.44m min x 7m\nSpacious double bedroom with carpeted flooring, built in wardrobes and eaves storage space\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.27m x 5.42m max\nLarge light filled double bedroom with built in wardrobes, carpeted flooring and eaves storage space\n\n"
